<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN" "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
  <overview>
    <p>An Azure DevOps checkout step with <code>persistCredentials: true</code>
    leaves its authentication token in Git configuration after the initial fetch.
    Subsequent steps can use that credential to access the repository with the
    permissions granted to the token.</p>
    <p>This is particularly risky when subsequent steps execute repository-controlled
    code or untrusted inputs. Self-hosted agents also require careful workspace
    isolation and cleanup. The setting does not by itself prove that the token has
    write permissions or that untrusted code is executed.</p>
    <p>This query reports explicit literal <code>true</code> settings (including
    quoted and case-insensitive spellings) on <code>checkout: self</code> and named
    repository checkouts in YAML pipelines and templates. It does not evaluate
    expressions, infer omitted values, or report <code>checkout: none</code>.
    Computed checkout targets are not reported. JSON, ARM, Terraform, and HCL
    templates are outside this query's scope. Conditional template branches are
    analyzed structurally; their reachability is not evaluated.</p>
  </overview>
  <recommendation>
    <p>Remove <code>persistCredentials</code> or set it to <code>false</code> unless
    later steps explicitly require authenticated Git operations. When credentials
    are necessary, isolate those operations from untrusted code, restrict the
    token's repository access and permissions, and ensure credentials are removed
    before the workspace is reused.</p>
  </recommendation>
  <example>
    <p>The first checkout leaves credentials available to the repository's build
    script. The second avoids retaining them after checkout.</p>
    <sample language="yaml"><![CDATA[
steps:
  # Not recommended: build code can access the checkout credential.
  - checkout: self
    persistCredentials: true
  - bash: ./build.sh

---
steps:
  # Recommended when subsequent steps do not need authenticated Git access.
  - checkout: self
    persistCredentials: false
  - bash: ./build.sh
]]></sample>
  </example>
  <references>
    <li>Microsoft Learn: <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/pipelines/yaml-schema/steps-checkout">steps.checkout definition</a>.</li>
    <li>Microsoft Learn: <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/pipelines/security/secure-access-to-repos">Secure access to repositories from pipelines</a>.</li>
    <li>Common Weakness Enumeration: <a href="https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html">CWE-522: Insufficiently Protected Credentials</a>.</li>
  </references>
</qhelp>
